#: src/library/index.md:3
msgid ""
"The library is where all your books live. Cadmus scans your device's storage "
"and keeps track of everything you've added, so you can browse, search, and "
"organize your collection right on the device."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/index.md:7
msgid "What's in this section"
msgstr ""

#: src/library/index.md:9
msgid ""
"[Importing books](importing.md) — how Cadmus finds and adds books to your "
"library"
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:1
msgid "Importing Books"
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:3
msgid ""
"Cadmus scans your device's storage and adds books to its database "
"automatically. This process is called **importing**."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:6
msgid "Automatic import on startup"
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:8
msgid ""
"Cadmus automatically imports books every time it starts. The import is "
"**incremental**: files whose modification time and file size haven't changed "
"since the last import are skipped, avoiding unnecessary re-fingerprinting. "
"Only new or modified files are processed, significantly improving startup "
"performance for large libraries."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:14
msgid ""
"Copy files to your device, restart the app, and they'll appear in your "
"library right away."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:17
msgid "Force full import"
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:19
msgid ""
"If you suspect the import cache is stale or corrupted, you can force a full "
"re-import:"
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:22
msgid "Open **Settings**."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:23
msgid "Navigate to the **Import** section."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:24
msgid "Tap **Force Full Import**."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:25
msgid "Confirm when prompted."
msgstr ""

#: src/library/importing.md:27
msgid ""
"This bypasses the incremental import cache and re-fingerprints all files in "
"your library directories. Be aware that this can take time and drain the "
"battery for large libraries, so keep your device plugged in while it runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:3
msgid ""
"When you open a book, Cadmus shows it in the **Reader**. How a book is "
"loaded depends on its type:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:6
msgid ""
"[Reflowable books](reflowable.md) — EPUB and HTML. Text is laid out to fit "
"your screen, font size, and margins."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:8
msgid ""
"[Paged books](paged.md) — comics (CBZ) and other page-based files such as "
"PDF. Each page is a fixed image or sheet."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:11
msgid "What stays in memory while you read"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:13
msgid "Cadmus uses two kinds of memory, depending on the book type:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:15
msgid ""
"**Screen pages (all books)** — Cadmus draws a page only when it needs to "
"show it (or to prepare a neighbor). It does **not** pre-draw the whole book. "
"At most **three** of those finished screen images stay in memory at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:18
msgid ""
"**HTML file layouts (reflowable only)** — the laid-out pages of each EPUB "
"HTML file you have already opened. See [Reflowable books](reflowable.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:21
msgid "Screen pages in memory"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:23
msgid ""
"Only the page you are on is required. Cadmus usually also keeps the previous "
"and next pages when they exist — **up to three** finished screen images "
"total. Pages outside that window are discarded from memory and drawn again "
"if you return to them."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:28
msgid ""
"In **fit-to-page** and **fit-to-width** zoom modes, Cadmus prepares the "
"previous and next pages in the background after a turn, so they are ready "
"when you move again."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:32
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"  prev[\"Previous page<br/>(in memory)\"] --- curr[\"Current page<br/>(in "
"memory)\"] --- next[\"Next page<br/>(in memory)\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:37
msgid "How Cadmus first opens the file still differs by mode:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:39
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TD\n"
"  open[Open a book] --> mode{Reading mode?}\n"
"  mode -->|Reflowable| reflow[\"Load HTML file list only<br/>then one HTML "
"file<br/>when you reach it\"]\n"
"  mode -->|Paged| paged[\"List pages only<br/>then decode one page<br/>when "
"you view it\"]\n"
"  reflow --> render[\"Keep up to 3<br/>screen pages in memory\"]\n"
"  paged --> render\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:48
msgid "Details:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:50
msgid "[Reflowable books](reflowable.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:51
msgid "[Paged books](paged.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:53 src/reader/reflowable.md:61 src/reader/paged.md:47
msgid "Related settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/index.md:55
msgid ""
"Shared reader options live under `[reader]` in "
"[Settings](../settings/index.md#reader), including what happens when you "
"finish a book, touch gestures, and screen refresh rates."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:3
msgid ""
"Reflowable books are EPUB files (and HTML documents). Cadmus lays the text "
"out to match your screen size, font, and margins."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:6
msgid "Opening a book"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:8
msgid ""
"An EPUB is a package of **HTML files** (plus styles and images) listed in "
"reading order. When you open one, Cadmus reads that file list and related "
"metadata. It does **not** load every HTML file at that moment."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:12
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TD\n"
"  open[Open EPUB] --> meta[\"Read HTML file list<br/>and metadata\"]\n"
"  meta --> idle[\"No HTML content files<br/>loaded yet\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:18
msgid "Opening an HTML file"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:20
msgid "When you first reach content that lives in a given HTML file, Cadmus:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:22
msgid ""
"Loads **that one HTML file** (and its stylesheets, unless document CSS is "
"ignored — see [Settings](../settings/index.md#readerignore-document-css))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:25
msgid ""
"Lays **the whole file** out into screen pages for your current font, "
"margins, and screen size."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:27
msgid "Keeps that file's **layout** in memory for the rest of the session."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:29
msgid ""
"So the unit Cadmus loads is an HTML file, not a table-of-contents chapter. "
"If the EPUB puts the entire book in a single HTML file, opening it loads and "
"lays out that whole book at once. If the book is split across many HTML "
"files, Cadmus loads each file only when you reach it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:34
msgid ""
"If you later return to an HTML file you already opened, Cadmus reuses the "
"stored layout instead of reading the file again. Visiting several files "
"means several layouts can sit in memory at once — still only the files you "
"have opened."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:38
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TD\n"
"  visit[\"Reach an HTML file\"] --> loaded{\"Layout already<br/>in "
"memory?\"}\n"
"  loaded -->|Yes| reuse[\"Reuse stored layout\"]\n"
"  loaded -->|No| html[\"Load that one<br/>HTML file\"]\n"
"  html --> layout[\"Layout the whole file<br/>into screen pages\"]\n"
"  layout --> store[\"Store that file layout<br/>in memory\"]\n"
"  reuse --> screen[\"Draw current<br/>screen page\"]\n"
"  store --> screen\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:49
msgid ""
"Changing reading options that affect layout (for example font family, font "
"size, margins, line height, text alignment, or whether document CSS is used) "
"clears **all** stored HTML file layouts. Cadmus rebuilds a file the next "
"time you reach it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:54
msgid ""
"Images referenced by an HTML file are loaded from the book when that file is "
"laid out or drawn."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:57
msgid ""
"On top of those file layouts, Cadmus still keeps **up to three screen "
"pages** in memory (current, and usually previous and next). See "
"[Reader](index.md#what-stays-in-memory-while-you-read)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:63
msgid ""
"These `[reader]` options affect reflowable layout. See "
"[Settings](../settings/index.md#reader) for full details:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:66
msgid ""
"[`font-path`](../settings/index.md#readerfont-path), "
"[`font-family`](../settings/index.md#readerfont-family), "
"[`font-size`](../settings/index.md#readerfont-size)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:69
msgid "[`text-align`](../settings/index.md#readertext-align)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:70
msgid "[`margin-width`](../settings/index.md#readermargin-width)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:71
msgid "[`line-height`](../settings/index.md#readerline-height)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:72
msgid "[`ignore-document-css`](../settings/index.md#readerignore-document-css)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:73
msgid "[`paragraph-breaker`](../settings/index.md#readerparagraph-breaker)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/reflowable.md:75
msgid "Installing and choosing fonts is covered in [Fonts](../fonts.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:3
msgid ""
"Paged books are made of fixed pages — typically one image or sheet per page. "
"Cadmus opens CBZ comic archives this way. Other page-based formats such as "
"PDF and standalone images use the same page-at-a-time model. DjVu books "
"follow a similar pattern through a separate decoder."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:8
msgid "Opening a CBZ"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:10
msgid ""
"A CBZ file is a zip archive of images. When you open one, Cadmus opens the "
"archive and builds an ordered **list of image file names** that count as "
"pages. It does **not** decode every image up front."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:14
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TD\n"
"  open[Open CBZ] --> zip[Open zip archive]\n"
"  zip --> names[\"List image<br/>page names\"]\n"
"  names --> idle[\"No page images<br/>decoded yet\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:21
msgid "Turning pages"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:23
msgid "When you view a page, Cadmus:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:25
msgid "Reads **that one page's image** from the archive."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:26
msgid "Decodes it into a rendered screen page."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:27
msgid ""
"Keeps **up to three** rendered pages in memory — typically the current page "
"plus the previous and next pages when they exist."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:30
msgid ""
"In **fit-to-page** and **fit-to-width** zoom modes, Cadmus prepares the "
"previous and next pages in the background after a turn. Pages outside that "
"window are not kept as finished screen images."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:34
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TD\n"
"  view[View page N] --> read[\"Read image N<br/>from archive\"]\n"
"  read --> decode[\"Decode into a<br/>rendered page\"]\n"
"  decode --> window[\"Memory: previous / current / next<br/>(up to 3 "
"rendered pages)\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:41
msgid ""
"The rest of the CBZ stays on disk as zip entries until you navigate to those "
"pages. Cadmus may also reuse a limited amount of lower-level decoded data "
"from the page engine, but the Reader itself only retains that small "
"rendered-page window. See "
"[Reader](index.md#what-stays-in-memory-while-you-read)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:49
msgid ""
"These `[reader]` options are especially relevant for paged books. See "
"[Settings](../settings/index.md#reader) for full details:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:52
msgid ""
"[`dithered-kinds`](../settings/index.md#readerdithered-kinds) — which file "
"types start with dithering on first open"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:54
msgid ""
"[`continuous-fit-to-width`](../settings/index.md#readercontinuous-fit-to-width) "
"— scroll mode used with fit-to-width zoom when a document is first opened"
msgstr ""

#: src/reader/paged.md:56
msgid ""
"[`refresh-rate`](../settings/index.md#readerrefresh-rate) — including "
"optional per-file-type overrides such as `cbz`"
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:3
msgid ""
"Cadmus can turn WiFi on when something needs the network, then turn it off "
"again when it is idle."
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:6
msgid "Modes"
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:8
msgid "Open the **WiFi** control in the top menu and choose one of:"
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:10
msgid ""
"**Off** — WiFi stays off. Features that need the network cannot turn it on "
"automatically; you must turn WiFi on yourself beforehand."
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:12
msgid "**Always On** — WiFi stays on."
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:13
msgid ""
"**Auto** — Cadmus turns WiFi on when something needs the network, then "
"powers it down after a period of inactivity."
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:16
msgid "Idle timeout"
msgstr ""

#: src/wifi.md:18
