#: src/auto-frontlight.md:3
msgid ""
"Cadmus can automatically adjust your frontlight's warmth and brightness "
"throughout the day based on the position of the sun at your location."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:8
msgid ""
"When enabled, Cadmus runs a background task that recalculates the ideal "
"frontlight levels every **5 minutes** and applies them immediately. The "
"first adjustment happens as soon as the feature starts, and then repeats on "
"every 5-minute mark."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:12
msgid "The adjustment has two dimensions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:14
msgid ""
"**Warmth** – zero warmth during the day, gradually ramping up to full warmth "
"over a 1.5-hour window around sunset, staying at full warmth through the "
"night, then ramping back down to zero over the 1.5-hour window before "
"sunrise."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:17
msgid ""
"**Brightness** – unchanged during the day (keeps whatever level you last "
"set). After sunset brightness drops to `auto-frontlight-night-brightness` "
"and stays there until sunrise."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:21
msgid "Enabling automatic adjustment"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:23
msgid "Open **Main Menu → Settings → General** and turn on **Auto Frontlight**."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:25
msgid "You can also enable it directly in your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:35
msgid ""
"See [`auto-frontlight`](settings/index.md#auto-frontlight) and related "
"entries in the Settings reference for all available options."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:38
msgid "Manual adjustments pause automation"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:40
msgid ""
"If you manually change the frontlight level while automatic adjustment is "
"running, Cadmus stops the background task so your chosen level is preserved. "
"Automatic adjustment resumes the next time the app is started."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:44
msgid "Location detection"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:46
msgid ""
"Sun position is calculated from your geographic coordinates. Cadmus obtains "
"these automatically during each [time sync](time-sync.md): the same "
"`ipapi.co` lookup that resolves your timezone also returns a latitude and "
"longitude, which are saved to `auto-frontlight-last-coordinates` in your "
"settings file."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:51
msgid ""
"If no coordinates are available yet (for example, before the first "
"successful time sync), automatic adjustment is skipped until a location is "
"known."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:54
msgid "Manual coordinates override"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:56
msgid ""
"If you prefer not to rely on IP-based location, or if the detected location "
"is inaccurate, you can set your own coordinates:"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:67
msgid "Manual coordinates take priority over auto-detected ones."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:69
msgid ""
"You can also edit this in **Main Menu → Settings → General** under **Auto "
"Frontlight Manual Coordinates**."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:72
msgid "Night brightness"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:74
msgid ""
"The brightness level used after sunset defaults to `1.0` (1%). You can raise "
"this if you find the screen too dim for nighttime reading:"
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:85
msgid "The value is a percentage from `0.0` to `100.0`."
msgstr ""

#: src/auto-frontlight.md:90
msgid ""
"When [automatic time syncing](time-sync.md) is enabled, a request is sent to "
"`ipapi.co` to resolve your timezone. That same response includes an "
"approximate latitude and longitude derived from your public IP address, "
"which Cadmus stores as `auto-frontlight-last-coordinates`."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:3
msgid ""
"Soft suspend lets Cadmus save battery between interactions by asking the "
"system to sleep when nothing important is running. It is optional and off by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:7
msgid ""
"This is separate from Auto Suspend (the timed “put the device to sleep” "
"setting) and from pressing the power button or closing a sleep cover. Auto "
"Suspend still applies when soft suspend is on: after the idle timeout Cadmus "
"prepares the touchscreen and other peripherals, then enters a deeper sleep "
"than the light nap used between taps."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:15
msgid ""
"When soft suspend is enabled, Cadmus tells the system which sleep target to "
"use (**Freeze** or **Memory**). While Cadmus is busy — handling a tap, using "
"the network, or running background work — it holds a wake lock so the device "
"stays awake. When that work finishes and nothing else needs attention, the "
"system can sleep."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:21
msgid "Enabling soft suspend"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:23
msgid ""
"Soft Suspend, the LED indicator, and release grace appear under **Settings → "
"Power** only when your device supports soft suspend. If those rows are "
"missing, Cadmus cannot soft-suspend on this hardware (for example the "
"desktop emulator)."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:27
msgid ""
"When the Soft Suspend setting is available, open **Main Menu → Settings → "
"Power** and set it to one of:"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:30
msgid "Option"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:30
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:32 src/soft-suspend.md:86
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:32
msgid "Soft suspend disabled (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:33
msgid "Freeze"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:33
msgid "Lighter sleep (when your device supports it)"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:34
msgid "Memory"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:34
msgid "Deeper sleep to RAM (when your device supports it)"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:36
msgid ""
"Only sleep targets your device supports appear in the list. You can also set "
"this in your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:47
msgid "Status LED indicator"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:49
msgid ""
"When soft suspend is available, under **Settings → Power** turn on **Use LED "
"to Indicate Soft Suspend** if you want the status LED on while soft suspend "
"is armed and the device is awake. The LED turns off when the device sleeps."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:53
msgid ""
"During **critical work** (for example a wireless update), the status LED may "
"**pulse** instead (long on, brief off). While it pulses, Cadmus blocks "
"sleep, power-off, and reboot until that work finishes or is cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:65
msgid "Release grace"
msgstr ""

#: src/soft-suspend.md:67
msgid ""
"When soft suspend is available, **Soft Suspend Release Grace** under "
"**Settings → Power** is how many seconds Cadmus keeps the wake lock after "
"the last busy activity ends. That avoids rapid sleep/wake when short gaps "
"fall between taps or background work. Set it to `0` to unlock immediately. "
"The default is five seconds."
msgstr ""

